    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate is headlined by **James Wood**, who stands as our clear-cut elite play with a 76.06 score. Matching up against Grant Holmes, **Wood** benefits from an elite 0.423 xwOBA and a favorable 4.71 xERA from the opposing arm. The combination of his top-of-the-order usage (+10% score boost) and high park factor makes him an essential start. We also see strong value in **Tyler Soderstrom** (67.73) and **Josh Naylor** (66.05); despite facing a veteran in Sonny Gray, both benefit significantly from a favorable park environment that boosts their offensive output. **Soderstrom** in particular capitalizes on the #4 spot in the order, making him our premier UTIL option for the day.\n\nWhile our roster is currently anchored by strong starters, the \"Lineup Pending\" status remains a logistical risk; should **Dalton Rushing** or **Austin Riley** drop further in the batting order than assumed, those scores will likely dip toward the marginal threshold. The most difficult decision rested on the marginal middle-infield tier, where **Edwin Arroyo** (45.14) just edged out his peers. The optimizer favored him due to a rare triple-threat of park, skill, and switch-hitting flexibility, even though his spot in the #8 hole suppresses his potential for runs. As for our bench, we remain cautious with **Vinnie Pasquantino** who is sidelined, while players like **Jose Caballero** and **Mickey Moniak** are excluded today due to lack of game activity, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active core to chase stolen bases and maintain our AVG ceiling.",
